@startuml Initialization

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor Black

!startsub INITIALIZATION
partition "Initialization (base)" {
    :Receive **Molecule**
    (atoms, per-atom charges, multiplicity,
     basis sets already validated);

    :Read **charge** = Σ atom.charge
    Read **multiplicity** from Molecule;

    :Compute total electron count
    <latex>N_{elec} = \sum_i Z_i + \text{charge}</latex>;

    :Convert coordinates
    Ångström → Bohr;
}

partition "HartreeFock (base)" {
    :Compute **n_basis**
    (total contracted Gaussians);

    :Register lazy **cgto** property
    (ContractedGaussianTypeOrbital built on first access
    via **ContractedGaussianTypeOrbital(molecule)**);

    note right
        For each atom, walk the hierarchical
        basis-set structure:
        **regions** (core, valence_inner, valence_outer)
        → angular momentum <latex>l</latex>
        → shells (exponents, coefficients)

        Each shell produces one
        <latex>\textbf{CGTO}(\mathbf{R}_A,\, l,\, \{\alpha_p\},\, \{d_p\})</latex>
        contributing <latex>2l + 1</latex> basis functions.
        Magnetic quantum number is resolved
        during integral evaluation.
    end note

    :Declare shared attributes
    <latex>N_{\alpha}</latex>, <latex>N_{\beta}</latex> (set by subclass);

    switch (HF Method?)
    case (RHF)
        partition "RHF – Restricted Closed-Shell" <<#LightGreen>> {
            if (<latex>N_{elec}</latex> is odd?) then (yes)
                :Raise **ValueError**
                "RHF requires even electrons"; <<#tomato>>
                end
            else (no)
            endif
            if (multiplicity ≠ 1?) then (yes)
                :Raise **ValueError**
                "RHF requires singlet"; <<#tomato>>
                end
            else (no)
            endif
            :<latex>N_{occ} = N_{elec} / 2</latex>
            <latex>N_{\alpha} = N_{\beta} = N_{occ}</latex>; <<#LightGreen>>
        }
    case (UHF)
        partition "UHF – Unrestricted" <<#LightCoral>> {
            :<latex>n_{unpaired} = M - 1</latex>; <<#LightCoral>>
            :<latex>N_{\beta} = (N_{elec} - n_{unpaired}) / 2</latex>
            <latex>N_{\alpha} = N_{\beta} + n_{unpaired}</latex>; <<#LightCoral>>
        }
    case (ROHF)
        partition "ROHF – Restricted Open-Shell" <<#LightYellow>> {
            :<latex>n_{unpaired} = M - 1</latex>
            <latex>n_{paired} = N_{elec} - n_{unpaired}</latex>; <<#LightYellow>>
            if (<latex>n_{paired}</latex> is odd?) then (yes)
                :Raise **ValueError**
                "Paired electrons not even"; <<#tomato>>
                end
            else (no)
            endif
            :<latex>N_{closed} = n_{paired} / 2</latex>
            <latex>N_{open}   = n_{unpaired}</latex>; <<#LightYellow>>
            :<latex>N_{\beta}  = N_{closed}</latex>
            <latex>N_{\alpha} = N_{closed} + N_{open}</latex>; <<#LightYellow>>
            :Verify <latex>M = N_{open} + 1</latex>; <<#LightYellow>>
        }
    endswitch
}

partition "NuclearRepulsionEnergy" #LightYellow {
    :Compute **Nuclear Repulsion Energy** <latex>E_{nuc}</latex>

    <latex>E_{nuc} = \sum_{A < B}^{N_{atoms}} \frac{Z_A \cdot Z_B}{|\mathbf{R}_A - \mathbf{R}_B|}</latex>

    Each pairwise term:
    <latex>E_{AB} = \frac{Z_A \cdot Z_B}{R_{AB}}</latex>
    where <latex>R_{AB} = \sqrt{(x_A-x_B)^2 + (y_A-y_B)^2 + (z_A-z_B)^2}</latex>

    **Physical interpretation:**
    Classical point-charge Coulomb repulsion
    between positively charged nuclei.
    This is a **constant scalar** (no electron dependence).

    **Units:** Hartree (atomic units)
    **Complexity:** <latex>O(N_{atoms}^2 / 2)</latex> pairs;

    note right
        **Key properties:**
        • Always **positive** (repulsive)
        • Independent of basis set
        • Independent of HF method
        • Added to <latex>E_{elec}</latex> at end
          to get <latex>E_{total}</latex>
        • Computed here (not in Integral Computation)
          because it requires **no basis functions**

        **Example (H₂ at 0.74 Å ≈ 1.4 Bohr):**
        <latex>E_{nuc} = \frac{1 \cdot 1}{1.4} \approx 0.714\,\mathrm{Ha}</latex>
    end note
}

:▼ **Transfer to Integral Computation →**
• Molecule (atoms in Bohr)
• **cgto** (lazy property, built on first access):
  flat list of CGTO shells, each carrying
  <latex>(\mathbf{R}_A,\, l,\, \{\alpha_p\},\, \{d_p\})</latex>
  and contributing <latex>2l + 1</latex> basis functions
• <latex>N_{elec}</latex>, charge, multiplicity
• n_basis (total number of basis functions)
• RHF: <latex>N_{occ}</latex>
  UHF: <latex>N_{\alpha}, N_{\beta}</latex>
  ROHF: <latex>N_{closed}, N_{open}</latex>
• hf_method ∈ {RHF, UHF, ROHF}
• <latex>E_{nuc}</latex> (scalar) → Finalization (<latex>E_{total} = E_{elec} + E_{nuc}</latex>); <<#LightBlue>>

stop
!endsub

legend right
    **Index Notation:**
    |= Index |= Range |= Description |
    | A | 1 … N_atoms | Atom index in molecule |
    | p | 1 … K | Primitive Gaussian index within a contraction |
    | μ | 1 … n_basis | Basis function index |
    ----
    **Symbol Legend:**
    |= Symbol |= Description |
    | Z_A | Atomic number of atom A |
    | charge | Sum of per-atom formal charges |
    | N_elec | Total number of electrons |
    | N_occ | Doubly-occupied orbitals (RHF) |
    | N_α | Alpha (spin-up) electrons |
    | N_β | Beta (spin-down) electrons |
    | N_closed | Doubly-occupied orbitals (ROHF) |
    | N_open | Singly-occupied orbitals (ROHF) |
    | M | Spin multiplicity (2S + 1) |
    | E_nuc | Nuclear repulsion energy (classical Coulomb) |
    | Bohr | Atomic unit of length (1 Bohr ≈ 0.529 Å) |
    ----
    **CGTO Parameters:**
    |= Symbol |= Description |
    | ContractedGaussianTypeOrbital | CGTO shell object (one per l value per atom) |
    | **R**_A | Atom centre position (Bohr) |
    | l | Angular momentum quantum number (0=s, 1=p, 2=d, …) |
    | K | Number of primitives in contraction |
    | α_p | Gaussian exponent of primitive p |
    | d_p | Contraction coefficient of primitive p |
    | n_basis | Total basis functions (sum of 2l+1 over all shells) |
    ----
    **HF Method Colors:**
    |<#LightGreen> RHF | Restricted Closed-Shell |
    |<#LightCoral> UHF | Unrestricted |
    |<#LightYellow> ROHF | Restricted Open-Shell |
    ----
    **Class Hierarchy:**
    Initialization → HartreeFock → { RHF, UHF, ROHF }
    NuclearRepulsionEnergy (standalone)
endlegend

@enduml
